From 0c22df041c65ac8ba80bb856a7cb66a5ae9d50b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:13:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] NOTICE-DEFER-4: the early PAUSE answer inside the
 MyMessageBox wait runs the same auth gate first -- confirmed bug from the
 review of 45d4f4d (hourly bug loop).
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

45d4f4d answered a notice's dialog.notifyAck ok at once inside MbWait after checking only the BtnPauseClick refusal; the held run's
auth gate (main-loop arm :4915, W906_NoteAuthNoticeGate) could still refuse after the page had closed the note -- e.g. auto-logout
(W906_A01AutoLogoutTick runs in the modal wait) or SpecialPanel lock while the box was up. The refusal went to a dead ticket, the
notice stayed live in C++ and keys read "擋關：通知框開著" again (the NOTICE-DEFER-1 symptom).

tools/wb_serve.cpp (same lines): MbWait runs W906_NoteAuthNoticeGate at the press, as golden DoPassword does: refused -> answered
refused, not held (the note stays; press again after dialog.auth); passed -> held and its id kept in g_w906NoticeGatePassed (:345) so
the :4915 arm skips the gate once (it spends the one-shot pass); the early ok only when NotifyAckDecide(g_alarmSlot, tag) == retire
and BtnPauseClick would not refuse. Global declaration on the :6554 line (MbWait is in the unnamed namespace).
Debug: wb_serve linked (program not running); NoticeAck passed; scan 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/wb_serve.cpp | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

